# rocm-ernic P4 control surface.
#
# ernic_p4 registers one misc device per emulated NIC -- /dev/ernic-p4 for the
# first, /dev/ernic-p4.N after it -- mode 0600 and owned by root, because
# whoever can open it can replace the P4 program and so decide what the NIC
# does with every frame and every RDMA operation.
#
# This image opens it to one group so a P4 test or benchmark needs no sudo.
# That is a choice for a test image, and it stays this narrow on purpose: a
# dedicated group, never world access. What a member can do is still bounded
# by the scope the operator gave the server (--p4-guest-scope).
#
# The rocm_ernic_setup role creates the group and adds the guest user.
SUBSYSTEM=="misc", KERNEL=="ernic-p4*", GROUP="ernic-p4", MODE="0660"
